% ============================================================================
% energy-forms — each named FORM of energy and the single defining token the
% source uses to describe it (adj-facts-stdlib, PHYSICS).
% ============================================================================
% One of the first organizing facts in physics: energy comes in NAMED FORMS,
% and each form is pinned by one characteristic word — chemical energy is about
% BONDS, nuclear energy is about the NUCLEUS, thermal energy is HEAT, motion
% energy is about things MOVING. Before a learner reasons about conservation of
% energy or converts one form into another, they first learn to NAME the forms
% and attach each to the word that defines it. Recall is a binding query:
%
%     ? energy_form_token(chemical, $T)      % bonds
%
% This is a native `table` (ADJ-TABLES RS-5): each `row` lowers to a ground
% relation `energy_form_token(form, token)` carrying THAT ROW'S OWN
% citation (RS-5e — before #14986 it was the table's single envelope), so
% the lookup above is the ordinary SLD binding query — the engine returns the
% defining token WITH its source, on the CPU, with zero model calls, and
% abstains on anything that is not one of the enumerated forms.
%
% The forms, as a little truth table (form → what the EIA sentence says → the
% single defining token we carry):
%
%     form            what the EIA definition says                 token
%     -------------   ------------------------------------------   -------------
%     chemical        "...stored in the bonds of atoms..."         bonds
%     mechanical      "...stored in objects by tension"            tension
%     nuclear         "...stored in the nucleus of an atom..."     nucleus
%     gravitational   "...stored in an object's height"            height
%     radiant         "...electromagnetic energy that travels..."  electromagnetic
%     thermal         "Thermal energy, or heat, is..."             heat
%     motion          "...stored in moving objects"                moving
%     electrical      "...charged particles, called electrons..."  electrons
%
% EIA groups these forms into two families — POTENTIAL energy (chemical,
% mechanical, nuclear, gravitational) and KINETIC energy (radiant, thermal,
% motion, electrical) — but the family split is not part of this table; the
% table is the single clean axis form → defining token. The query also runs
% BACKWARD — bind the token and recall the form it defines:
%
%     ? energy_form_token($F, heat)          % thermal — reverse recall
%
% Every `token` is a SINGLE lowercase atom that appears VERBATIM inside that
% form's own EIA definition sentence (quoted per-row in the provenance block
% below), never a synonym or a word the source does not use. Something that is
% not one of the enumerated forms — magnetic energy, for instance, which is real
% physics but is NOT one of the forms this EIA page names — has no row, so a
% recall on it ABSTAINS rather than inventing a token. That honest-abstention
% property is what makes the table safe to reason from.
%
% ONE ABSTENTION HERE IS NOT HONEST, AND IS DISCLOSED RATHER THAN QUIETLY LEFT.
% The page names NINE forms; this table has eight. `sound` abstains even though
% the same page defines it, once, in prose: "Sound is energy moving through
% substances in longitudinal (compression or rarefaction) waves." That is a
% false negative against this table's OWN source, not a limit of the source.
% The sibling `energy-form-family.adj` already discloses the same gap. Adding
% the row is ordinary work and is tracked separately — it is a change to what
% this table CLAIMS, which does not belong in a provenance conversion.
%
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Provenance. EVERY ROW CARRIES ITS OWN DEFINING SENTENCE, below, in the row's
% `{ ... }` block (ADJ-TABLES RS-5e) — read those, not a restatement here. One
% page, one tier: the U.S. Energy Information Administration's "Forms of
% energy" explainer, a primary U.S. government source, so `trust authoritative`.
%
% WHAT #14986 CHANGED. The envelope was the CHEMICAL sentence, so a recall of
% `electrical` came back warranted by a sentence about the bonds of atoms and
% molecules. The envelope now carries the page's framing sentence, which
% warrants no row — and the test pins its WORDING against this file, rather
% than disclosing it as unreachable the way the earlier entries in this cascade
% had to.
%
% SAME PAGE, DIFFERENT ANSWER FROM ITS SIBLING. `physics/energy-form-family.adj`
% cites this same page and is NOT convertible: there the potential/kinetic
% grouping lives in a SECTION HEADING and no sentence assigns a form to a
% family, so its rows would need `trust inferred` or a very long contiguous
% quote. That is recorded on #15139. This table asks what each form IS, which
% the page states in prose, one sentence per form. The question is per table,
% not per page.
%
% ONE VARIANT HEAD, kept as the page writes it: "Thermal energy, or heat, is
% the energy that comes from atoms and molecules moving in a substance." A
% probe that required a plain "Thermal energy is..." reported this row as
% having no defining sentence at all — the probe's prefix test, not the page.
% A mutant that normalises the head reddens.
%
% (See ../README.md; feedback_nothing_human_authored,
% feedback_adj_only_shipped_artifacts.)
% ============================================================================

table energy_form_token {
    columns form, token

    row (chemical, bonds) {
        % This sentence was the table's whole envelope, so it also
        % warranted the seven rows below it.
        source "Chemical energy is energy stored in the bonds of atoms and molecules."
    }
    row (mechanical, tension) {
        source "Mechanical energy is energy stored in objects by tension."
    }
    row (nuclear, nucleus) {
        source "Nuclear energy is energy stored in the nucleus of an atom—the energy that holds the nucleus together."
    }
    row (gravitational, height) {
        source "Gravitational energy is energy stored in an object's height."
    }
    row (radiant, electromagnetic) {
        source "Radiant energy is electromagnetic energy that travels in transverse waves."
    }
    row (thermal, heat) {
        % Variant head: the page writes "Thermal energy, or heat,
        % is...", not "Thermal energy is...". A probe that required
        % the plain form reported this row as having no defining
        % sentence -- the probe's prefix test, not the page. Same
        % shape as gravitropism and electrotropism in
        % biology/plant-tropisms.adj (#15176).
        source "Thermal energy, or heat, is the energy that comes from atoms and molecules moving in a substance."
    }
    row (motion, moving) {
        source "Motion energy is energy stored in moving objects."
    }
    row (electrical, electrons) {
        source "Electrical energy is delivered by tiny, charged particles, called electrons, that typically move through a wire."
    }

    % The envelope is the FRAMING span -- that energy comes in many
    % forms at all. It defends the TABLE and warrants no row. Until
    % #14986 it was the CHEMICAL row's own sentence.
    source "Many forms of energy exist, but energy is either potential energy or kinetic energy."
    locator "https://www.eia.gov/energyexplained/what-is-energy/forms-of-energy.php"
    trust authoritative
}
